SUCCESS. Committed `beee58774` on `w2_stale-race`.

**What changed** — one source file, `internal/autoimport/autoimport.go`. `AutoImportIfNewer` (the RPC/daemon auto-import path, called from `internal/rpc/server_export_import_auto.go:358`) no longer compares the file's hash to `jsonl_content_hash` itself. It now asks `jsonlpub.ContentState`, with the same mapping `cmd/bd/autoflush.go` got in Round 3: Fresh skips (and still calls `recordImport` so a mtime-only change stops looking new), NoFile skips, Diverged and NoMetadata import, and a `ContentState` error becomes NoMetadata so unreadable metadata recovers by importing instead of going quiet. The bd-39o `last_import_hash` fallback wasn't dropped, it moved into `jsonlpub.readCommitted` where the protocol owns it. The parsed-bytes hash rule and everything below the decision are untouched.

**Regression test** — `TestAutoImportIfNewer_PendingHashIsFresh` in `internal/autoimport/autoimport_test.go`: file matches `jsonl_pending_hash`, `jsonl_content_hash` holds a different hash. Pre-fix FAIL ("re-imported content the database had already published"), post-fix PASS. Pre-fix proof taken by temporarily restoring the old comparison with the Edit tool, no `git checkout`.

**Gates** — both green. Gate 1 exit 0, all five packages ok. Gate 2: `comm -13 baseline_failures.txt post3_failures.txt` printed nothing; the only failures are the two pre-existing read-only-git-config environmental ones already in the baseline. Logs in `work/w2_stale-race/builds/r4_*.log`, artifacts in `artifacts/post3*`.

**Class closure** — the grep leaves six non-test, non-`jsonlpub` hits: four are comments (`internal/importer/importer.go:69`, `cmd/bd/import_shared.go:196`, `cmd/bd/autoflush.go:108`, and my new comment), plus the two known non-defects. The daemon health check at `cmd/bd/daemon_event_loop.go:242` discards both metadata values and inspects only `err` — nothing is compared to a file hash and only a log line follows, so it asks "is metadata readable", not "is the file fresh". `updateExportMetadata` at `cmd/bd/daemon_sync.go:281` only calls `SetMetadata` for multi-repo suffixed keys and is unreachable without a multi-repo config; it's a writer that decides nothing, and the plan keeps multi-repo metadata byte-identical. No freshness decision remains outside tests and `internal/jsonlpub`.

**Two observations, neither changed.** `gofmt -l` flags the touched file, but the sole issue is a pre-existing trailing-whitespace line in `showRemapping` (line 185), unrelated to this change and left out of the commit. And the preserved Fresh-path `recordImport` keeps a narrow race: if the file is replaced between `os.ReadFile` and `ContentState`, the recorded hash describes bytes no longer on disk — self-healing, since the next reader sees Diverged and imports.
